# LS_COLORS entries, one per line. user-shell.nix joins them with ":" at build
# time and exports the result, so changes apply on the next rebuild switch.
#
# Each line is `<key>=<style>` where <key> is a two-letter file class or a
# *glob, and <style> is a ";"-separated list of ANSI SGR attributes:
#
#   0       default foreground
#   1       bold
#   2       dim
#   3       italic
#   4       underline
#   30-37   foreground from palette slot 0-7
#           (black, red, green, yellow, blue, magenta, cyan, white)
#   90-97   foreground from bright slot 8-15
#   38;5;N  foreground from palette slot N (38;5;8 = gray, 38;5;11 = bright
#           yellow); clearer than 90-97 when the slot number matters
#
# Attributes compose: "1;4;32" = bold underlined green. Palette slots only, no
# truecolor, so everything follows the plain dark/light terminal palettes.
#
# The most specific pattern wins. This file is the single source of truth for
# listing colors: lines prefixed "eza:" are routed into EZA_COLORS instead of
# LS_COLORS (see the last section), so eza renders files exactly like ls does,
# plus its own UI colors on top.
#
# Seeded from `vivid generate ansi` with the `*.ext=0` no-op entries stripped.
# Deviations from the seed: agent/readme docs in bright yellow, lockfiles gray,
# and the image and build-file groups promoted from eza's built-in styles.

# File classes: di=directory, ln=symlink, or=orphaned symlink, mi=missing link
# target, ex=executable, pi=fifo, so=socket, do=door, bd/cd=block/char device,
# st/tw/ow=sticky/other-writable dirs, sg/su=setgid/setuid.
di=0;34
ln=3;36
or=3;31
mi=1;31
ex=1;33
pi=0;35
so=1;35
do=1;35
bd=1;4;32
cd=1;32
st=1;34
tw=1;4;34
ow=4;34
sg=1;4;33
su=1;4;33

